slayer</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artpage-fartpage"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/lynch3.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="lynch3.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <hr /> <h1><span>Q&amp;A:</span></h1> <h2><span>Q: Can I replace a blurb that you wrote for one of my articles with my own? I'm not satisfied with it.</span></h2> <p>A: Absolutely. You will always have that option at any point.</p> <h2><span>Q: I noticed an error/typo/incorrect information and wish to correct it. May I?</span></h2> <p>A: Sure! If the changes are not limited to your own article(s) and/or are substantial changes across multiple entries, you should post in that month's discussion page and then make the changes.</p> <h2><span>Q: I wrote an article and it seems to have stuck. Can I send a blurb of mine to one of the frequent collaborators?</span></h2> <p>A: Yup! It's much easier if you come to us about it, and it gives you the control over what you want shown on the news page.</p> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>« <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-09-2020">September 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-10-2020">October 2020</a></span> | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-11-2020">November 2020</a> »</strong></p> </div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-