&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;« &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/news-09-2020&quot;&gt;September 2020&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/news-10-2020&quot;&gt;October 2020&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; | &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/news-11-2020&quot;&gt;November 2020&lt;/a&gt; »&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:75%;&quot;&gt;This is a series showing off news from the site, articles from the past month&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-29134-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, and fan-content for you to check out and discover! Be sure to leave a comment with your thoughts!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span&gt;Fandom Stuff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SCP-FR (French language branch of the SCP Foundation) is running &lt;a href=&quot;http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/le-concours-des-404-ans&quot;&gt;a contest&lt;/a&gt; for the SCP-404-FR slot. Participants are asked to write about &amp;quot;An error, something that caused one or the consequences of one&amp;quot;. The visual design of the contest hub is worth checking out whether you speak French or not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SCP-EN (English, this wiki) is conducting another &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/instagram-fan-art-contest-fall-2020&quot;&gt;Instagram Fan Art Contest&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SCP-PL (Polish) is running the inventive &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-pl.wikidot.com/rezurekcja-usunietych&quot;&gt;Resurrecting The Deleted&lt;/a&gt; contest. Participants pick a title of a work from the Deletions Log, and write an article using said title.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SCP-KO (Korean) finished its latest &lt;a href=&quot;http://ko.scp-wiki.net/bimonthly-contests-2020#toc4&quot;&gt;bimonthly contest&lt;/a&gt;. The theme of the contest was &amp;quot;Language&amp;quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SCP-DE (German) concluded its second &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki-de.wikidot.com/halloween-wettbewerb-2020&quot;&gt;Halloween contest&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SCP-IT (Italian) also ran a &lt;a href=&quot;http://fondazionescp.wikidot.com/concorso-halloween-2020-dr-zeno&quot;&gt;Halloween contest&lt;/a&gt; this month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span&gt;Featured Articles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5380&quot;&gt;SCP-5380&lt;/a&gt; (by chiifu): My World [Featured by Truc Linh and Quadraginta]&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;As a result, the entire mall was showered with snowflakes and small paper hearts.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/the-significant-others-part-a&quot;&gt;The Significant Others, Part &amp;quot;A&amp;quot;&lt;/a&gt; by HarryBlank [Featured by weizhong, Grigori Karpin, and PlaguePJP]&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;&amp;quot;I&#039;m not a subject in containment,&amp;quot; said Phil.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Azad grinned. &amp;quot;Sure you&#039;re not.&amp;quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/deer-and-the-overseers&quot;&gt;Deer And The Overseers&lt;/a&gt; &lt;tt&gt;[Deer College]&lt;/tt&gt; by stormbreath [Featured by The Pighead, Marcelles_Raynes, and Pedagon]&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;In honor of the termination of the old Council, I&#039;ll be looking at the history of Deer&#039;s interactions with them…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span&gt;Reviewer&#039;s Spotlight Articles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5462&quot;&gt;SCP-5462&lt;/a&gt; (Misery is the State of Every Soul Burdened by Mortality.) by Cerastes [Selected by Cerastes]&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;[…] commonly referred to as his Black Paintings due to their emotionally disturbing contents, themes, and use of dark colours.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5456&quot;&gt;SCP-5456&lt;/a&gt; (Sweatmother) by faminepulse [Selected by Grigori Karpin]&lt;br /&gt;
