					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>« <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-10-2020">October 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-11-2020">November 2020</a></span> | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-12-2020">December 2020</a> »</strong></p> </div> <p><span style="font-size:75%;">This is a series showing off news from the site, articles from the past month<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-977682-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>, and fan-content for you to check out and discover! Be sure to leave a comment with your thoughts!</span></p> <h4><span>Fandom Stuff</span></h4> <ul> <li>SCP-FR (French language branch of the SCP Foundation) is running <a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/le-concours-des-404-ans">a contest</a> for the SCP-404-FR slot. Participants are asked to write about &quot;An error, something that caused one or the consequences of one&quot;. The visual design of the contest hub is worth checking out whether you speak French or not.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-EN (English, this wiki) is conducting another <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/instagram-fan-art-contest-fall-2020">Instagram Fan Art Contest</a>.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-PL (Polish) is running the inventive <a href="http://scp-pl.wikidot.com/rezurekcja-usunietych">Resurrecting The Deleted</a> contest. Participants pick a title of a work from the Deletions Log, and write an article using said title.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-KO (Korean) finished its latest <a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/bimonthly-contests-2020#toc4">bimonthly contest</a>. The theme of the contest was &quot;Language&quot;.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-DE (German) concluded its second <a href="http://scp-wiki-de.wikidot.com/halloween-wettbewerb-2020">Halloween contest</a>.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-IT (Italian) also ran a <a href="http://fondazionescp.wikidot.com/concorso-halloween-2020-dr-zeno">Halloween contest</a> this month.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Featured Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5380">SCP-5380</a> (by chiifu): My World [Featured by Truc Linh and Quadraginta]<br /> <em>As a result, the entire mall was showered with snowflakes and small paper hearts.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-significant-others-part-a">The Significant Others, Part &quot;A&quot;</a> by HarryBlank [Featured by weizhong, Grigori Karpin, and PlaguePJP]<br /> <em>&quot;I'm not a subject in containment,&quot; said Phil.</em><br /> <em>Azad grinned. &quot;Sure you're not.&quot;</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/deer-and-the-overseers">Deer And The Overseers</a> <tt>[Deer College]</tt> by stormbreath [Featured by The Pighead, Marcelles_Raynes, and Pedagon]<br /> <em>In honor of the termination of the old Council, I'll be looking at the history of Deer's interactions with them…</em></li> </ul> <h4><span>Reviewer's Spotlight Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5462">SCP-5462</a> (Misery is the State of Every Soul Burdened by Mortality.) by Cerastes [Selected by Cerastes]<br /> <em>[…] commonly referred to as his Black Paintings due to their emotionally disturbing contents, themes, and use of dark colours.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5456">SCP-5456</a> (Sweatmother) by faminepulse [Selected by Grigori Karpin]<br /> <em>“We can be human, yeah we can be respectful, but we can't tolerate chaos. You</em> have <em>to be our<sup>[sic]</sup> own dads.”</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4423">SCP-4423</a> (StepDemon) by Dyslexion [Selected by Sonderance]<br /> <em>SCP-4423 is a Tartarean-Class demonic entity that manifests during sleep paralysis.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5788">SCP-5788</a> (Partners in sync) by Riemann [Selected by OCuin]<br /> <em>The integration of SCP-5788 into the plumbing of the kitchen makes removal and characterisation difficult.</em></li> </ul> <div id="toc" class="floatright"> <div id="toc-action-bar"><a href="javascript:;" >Fold</a><a style="display: none" href="javascript:;" >Unfold</a></div> <div class="title">Table of Contents</div> <div id="toc-list"> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc0">Week of November 1st:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc1">Week of November 8th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc2">Week of November 15th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 4em;"><a href="#toc3">*GoI Formats</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc4">Week of November 22nd:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc5">Fanart</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p>You will notice little '📈' emojis beside some articles. That denotes SCP articles which were under 30 and tales which were under 20 when this edition of site news was posted. Give them a little love! Speaking from personal experience, the most frustrating thing that can happen to an article is not deletion, but stagnating below 20 without any comments. So try to read, vote, and comment on these articles! They're often hidden gems :)</p> <h3><span>Week of November 1st:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5178">SCP-5178</a> (&quot;Eat The Sun with Seth Uhar&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by DecoyMesa.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5733">SCP-5733</a> (&quot;Knife. Scream. Cut to Black.&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Dysadron.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5414">SCP-5414</a> (&quot;Clouds Only Dreamt&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Barbarous Bread.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5170">SCP-5170</a> (&quot;<strong>Pattern Screamer, Esq.</strong> 💼⚖️&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Amytato.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5598">SCP-5598</a> (&quot;I, Eurydice Ferlinghetti&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by LordStonefish.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5146">SCP-5146</a> (&quot;Perfect Territory&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by daviiid.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5132">SCP-5132</a> (&quot;The Kids Aren't Alright&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Raddagher.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5957">SCP-5957</a> (&quot;A Baleful Light&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Grigori Karpin.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/eating-honey-in-the-rain">Eating Honey in the Rain</a> - &quot;<em>Oh, how gentle the fruit is from the Moon's sweet carcass, as if harvested from the giant maw of a bee stung beast</em>&quot; Written by Amelia Wright.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/austin-aggy-genadew">Austin “Aggy” Genadew</a> - &quot;<em>What am I supposed to do with apples?</em>&quot; Written by DarkStuff.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/alone-in-a-sea-of-voices">Alone in a Sea of Voices</a> - <em>&quot;Connection Approved. Welcome to Oneiroi West, we hope you enjoy your stay!&quot;</em> Written by Dr Moned.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/icon-documents">Regular documents from the Iconography Division</a> - &quot;<em>The primary purpose of the Iconography Division is to suppress, record, study, and utilize anomalous imagery and symbolism in service of the Foundation's mission.</em>&quot; Written by EstrellaYoshte.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/behind-the-times">Behind The Times</a> - &quot;<em>Whatever it was, it certainly wasn’t a mugging. His cash is still in his wallet</em>&quot; Written by Nephews of Liberty.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-little-bunnys-doctor">A Little Bunny's Doctor</a> - &quot;<em>When I was younger, I frequently spent time in the hospital due to my undeveloped immune system.</em>&quot; Written by Ellie3.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Misc</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/interviewing-icons-djoric">Interviewing Icons - Djoric</a> - &quot;Djoric as interviewed by WhiteGuard.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/uau112020">Underread and Underrated November 2020</a> - Written by Elogee FishTruck.</li> </ul> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <h3><span>Week of November 8th:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5506">SCP-5506</a> (&quot;The Best Part Of Waking Up Is Manifesting a New God&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by MalyceGraves.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5594">SCP-5594</a> (&quot;Fine Dine and Good Spirits&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by PlaguePJP.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5495">EXTDOC-5495</a> (&quot;THE GHAZNI INCIDENT.&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Rounderhouse.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5685">SCP-5685</a> (&quot;The Airstream Con&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by RadioactiveRADS.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-0000-ex">SCP-0000-EX</a> (&quot;%%actual-title%%&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Ralliston.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5366">SCP-5366</a> (&quot;Until death do us part and every day after&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Pedagon.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5348">SCP-5348</a> (&quot;Mama Ambrose's Creamy Mushroom Bisque&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Elunerazim.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5583">SCP-5583</a> (&quot;Skippy the Unicorn Has Had Enough of Your Shit&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Nickthebrick1.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5118">SCP-5118</a> (&quot;Forever a Good Boy&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by deathbygin.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/drcoolbad">Dr.Coolbad Destroys the Economy</a> - &quot;<em>It was an office supply mogul’s paradise.</em>&quot; Written by Raddagher.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/i-was-a-teenage-shoggoth">i was a teenage shoggoth (Ween cover)</a> - &quot;<em>If, four thousand years ago, you'd told the Jack of Spades he'd be doing manual labor for a Xian criminal, he probably wouldn't have believed you.</em>&quot; Written by UraniumEmpire.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/coming-cold">Coming Cold</a> - &quot;<em>Nobody noticed it over the sudden cold.</em>&quot; Written by Brewsterion 1017.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Misc</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/object-class-podcast">Object Class: Podcast</a> - Two local nerds host a podcast! Written by Captain Kirby.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/t">TSATPWTCOTTTADC's workbench</a> - It's TSATPWTCOTTTADC's workbench!</li> </ul> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <h3><span>Week of November 15th:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5158">SCP-5158</a> (&quot;Lacum Lacrimarum&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by JackalRelated.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5944">SCP-5944</a> (&quot;Dead Men Tell No Tales&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Harvoable .</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5787">SCP-5787</a> (&quot;Bad Things Happen in Philadelphia&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by PlaguePJP.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5510">SCP-5510</a> (&quot;Universal Remote&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by aismallard.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5917">SCP-5917</a> (&quot;The Map of the Multiverse&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by chaucer345.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5661">SCP-5661</a> (&quot;The Devil and the Maiden&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by stormbreath.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3651">SCP-3651</a> (&quot;Chalk Children&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by J Dune.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chapter-7-the-woman-who-wasn-t-there">The Woman Who Wasn't There</a> - &quot;<em>Allison looked down at the hand she had just used to rewrite Robert; a hat was in it, solid black, something that looked vaguely like a fedora, but with a far wider brim.</em>&quot; Written by Ihp.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chapter-6-the-taking-of-dr-sinclair">The Taking of Dr. Sinclair</a> - &quot;<em>Dr. Katherine Sinclair practically threw the mug of coffee in her face.</em>&quot; Written by Ihp.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/i-say-this-that-you-suffer">i say this that you suffer</a> - &quot;<em>- then, perhaps, is when she steps from the umbra of girl.</em>&quot; Written by OriCat.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ronald-reagan-cut-up-while-rapping">RONALD REAGAN CUT UP WHILE RAPPING</a> - &quot;<em>Thanks I hate it.</em>&quot; Written by LordStonefish.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/repatriation">Repatriation</a> - &quot;<em>All she could do was imagine the hunger in the voice promising to wait for her.</em>&quot; Written by Grigori Karpin.</li> </ul> <h4><span>*GoI Formats</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/la-rue-posts-willie-s-shine">LaRue Post - Willie's shine</a> - [GOIname] &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Vivarium.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Misc</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/more-acs-icons">If you want more cool ACS secondary class icons</a> - Written by Dr Fishbone.</li> </ul> <h3><span>Week of November 22nd:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4604">SCP-4604</a> (&quot;Disillusionment&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by TL333s.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5936">SCP-5936</a> (&quot;Those that do not wish to be forgotten&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Ralliston.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4576">SCP-4576</a> (&quot;Protective Prickly Pal, Prixors&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by Quadraginta.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5949">SCP-5949</a> (&quot;Drugs and Webpages at Site-69&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by JakdragonX.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5702">SCP-5702</a> (&quot;'www.wikiflick.███'&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by LordStonefish.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/from-syllables-to-lines-to-imagination">From syllables to lines to imagination</a> - &quot;<em>Am hungry, gimme a munchy!</em>&quot; Written by Sirslash47.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/fox-hunt">Fox Hunt</a> - &quot;<em>If you can point me in the direction of an expert, or provide some insight yourself, I would be in your debt.</em>&quot; Written by Grigori Karpin.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/t-aint-no-sin">T'Ain't No Sin</a> - &quot;<em>Uwuu, you stiww have skin?! Teehee! No wowwies, Imma hewp you get wid of it</em>&quot; Written by daveyoufool.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chef-s-table">Chef's Table</a> - &quot;<em>When I'm cooking for myself, my diet goes to shit.</em>&quot; Written by Dysadron.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/patience">Patience</a> - &quot;<em>None of them had a ghostly Klavigar that could be anywhere or anyone she wanted to be, working tirelessly to lay the foundation.</em>&quot; Written by MalyceGraves.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Misc</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/form-5118-e-proposal-for-reclassification">Form 5118-E: Proposal for Reclassification</a> - Written by deathbygin.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/experiment-log-5702">Experiment Log 5702</a> - Written by LordStonefish.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> - Written by TheMightyMcB.</li> </ul> <h3><span>Fanart</span></h3> <h5><span>Here you will find a selection of artists whose art output is worth following. The thumbnails are clickable.</span></h5> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size:larger;"><a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/CHNcjPZFQwH/">Instagram Art Contest</a></span> by sk0rpt, bubblebaphomet, cookie_cream13, issued_pnts, philltheguy, Rigen</p> <span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(0, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(0, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">Instagram Art Contest</span><a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/CHNcjPZFQwH/"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/Contest.JPG" style="width:33%;" alt="Contest.JPG" class="image" /></a></span> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <hr /> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size:larger;"><a href="https://aminoapps.com/c/scp-foundation/page/user/festivebones/WMoB_2gSkfWwvZl0vP0jdkn2bzbkWNJ16Ir">FestiveBone's Amino Page</a></span> by FestiveBones</p> <span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(80, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(80, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">Red Reality</span><a href="https://aminoapps.com/c/scp-foundation/page/blog/red-reality/gE46_aNU6u66x2k1P5LE3KvbzVadVxrNL"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/bones1.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="bones1.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(30, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(30, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">&quot;The Startling Statue&quot;</span><a href="https://aminoapps.com/c/scp-foundation/page/blog/the-startling-statue/kjb3_rpiGupnwR54bJYpdwYXBYRaj1WjkD"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/bones2.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="bones2.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(240, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(240, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">“OwO What’s This?”</span><a href="https://aminoapps.com/c/scp-foundation/page/blog/owo-whats-this/YlNa_LZibu0Kp7pWjQDvpj28dEW50lda3l"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/bones3.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="bones3.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span> <hr /> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size:larger;"><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/klakkr-art">Klakkr's Artwork</a></span> by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/klakkr" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3304498&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607049802" alt="Klakkr" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3304498)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/klakkr" >Klakkr</a></span></p> <span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(80, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(80, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">SCP-682</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/klakkr-art"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/klakkr1.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="klakkr1.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(30, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(30, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">SCP-1762</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/klakkr-art"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/klakkr2.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="klakkr2.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(240, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(240, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">SCP-939</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/klakkr-art"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/klakkr3.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="klakkr3.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span> <hr /> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size:larger;"><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artpage-fartpage">lynch artpage fartpage</a></span> by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stephlynch" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1802367&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607049802" alt="stephlynch" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1802367)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stephlynch" >stephlynch</a></span></p> <span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(80, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(80, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">Tik Tak Tow</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artpage-fartpage"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/lynch1.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="lynch1.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(30, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(30, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">Gate Guardian</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artpage-fartpage"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/lynch2.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="lynch2.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><span class="hover"><span style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, hsla(240, 25%, 50%, 0.75) 0%, hsla(240, 25%, 50%, 1) 50%);">The Dragonslayer</span><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artpage-fartpage"><img src="http://smlt.wikidot.com/local--files/collab:drakimoto:art-stuff/lynch3.jpg" style="width:33%;" alt="lynch3.jpg" class="image" /></a></span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <hr /> <h1><span>Q&amp;A:</span></h1> <h2><span>Q: Can I replace a blurb that you wrote for one of my articles with my own? I'm not satisfied with it.</span></h2> <p>A: Absolutely. You will always have that option at any point.</p> <h2><span>Q: I noticed an error/typo/incorrect information and wish to correct it. May I?</span></h2> <p>A: Sure! If the changes are not limited to your own article(s) and/or are substantial changes across multiple entries, you should post in that month's discussion page and then make the changes.</p> <h2><span>Q: I wrote an article and it seems to have stuck. Can I send a blurb of mine to one of the frequent collaborators?</span></h2> <p>A: Yup! It's much easier if you come to us about it, and it gives you the control over what you want shown on the news page.</p> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>« <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-10-2020">October 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-11-2020">November 2020</a></span> | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-12-2020">December 2020</a> »</strong></p> </div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <hr /> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/a-random-day" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1841781&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607049802" alt="A Random Day" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1841781)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/a-random-day" >A Random Day</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-977682-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. with a rating above 0</div> </div> 
